    "sha": "3d16225d34a2192c68391e2217336900bd14d320",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDNkMTYyMjVkMzRhMjE5MmM2ODM5MWUyMjE3MzM2OTAwYmQxNGQzMjA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "jnz-1",
        "email": "jnz-1@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T01:31:04Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "jnz-1",
        "email": "jnz-1@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T01:31:04Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): two orientation dropdowns, one section everywhere (#771)\n\nThe setup orientation UI is two dropdowns: Plane orientation (Axes\ndefault, Points, Face, Manual, Cylinder angle) and Orientation point\n(model box / stock box / manual vertex), each expanding its method's\ncontrols below it. One component (setup_orient_pick::section)\nmounted on the Setups overview AND each setup's Settings page - same\ndropdowns, same options, same look; the old rows keep their own entry\npoints and draw verbatim as the expanded content.\n\nCylinder angle (the completing piece): one pick on a bore's or\ncylinder's curved wall names its axis from the wall's own facet\nnormals (any two non-parallel wall normals cross exactly along it;\nevery other normal is verified - a mixed patch is refused by name,\nnever misread). The axis lands on a chosen world axis, turned by an\nangle about it, the part turning about its bounds centre; the work\noffset is never touched.\n\nOrientation point: the parts' bounds or the setup's stock (corner or\ncentre) or a picked vertex places the named setup's WCS origin\n(SetWcsOrigin::for_setup), the rotation kept - the frame comes from\nthe plane side. Each setup places its own WCS, never the active\none's; undoable.\n\nTests: crates/app/tests/orient_dropdowns.rs (9) - the tilted\ncylinder's axis lands on Z/X/Y end to end, the 90-degree angle\nswings about the landed axis and keeps it put, flat face / edge / NaN\nangle refused by name, model and stock box corner/centre, rotation\nkept, per-setup placement, undo, missing model/stock refused by name.\nUI: structural twin rewritten for the dropdowns; setup_picks_disarm\nswitches the dropdown first (switch_plane_method), all 8 green.\nBattery green: ui 37, orient 9, align_axes 9, axis_align 10,\nplane_align 9, points_align 8, turn_pivot 5; clippy clean.\n\nFixes #771",
